  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Shorshe"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " means mustard in Bengali, captured in "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "shorshe ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "shorshe"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". This dish is traditionally made with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "ilish ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "ilish"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", a fatty river fish. Cod stands in for it here. The key element is the sharp "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "mustard paste",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "mustard-paste"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " made from ground mustard seeds, which gives the dish its characteristic pungency."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use a mix of black and yellow mustard seeds. Too many black seeds can make the paste very bitter. Soak the seeds for 30 minutes before grinding to reduce bitterness."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "cod-fillet",
              "amount": 600,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "cut into thick slices",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "mustard-seeds",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": "soaked 30 minutes, then ground to paste",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "chilli-green",
              "amount": 4,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": "2 for the paste, 2 left whole",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "turmeric",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": "divided",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "nigella-seeds",
              "amount": 0.5,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "vegetable-oil",
              "amount": 3,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": "mustard oil if available",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "plain-yoghurt",
              "amount": 50,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "whisked, optional to soften the mustard",
              "isOptional": true,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "sea-salt-fine",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ],
          "defaultServings": 4
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Grind soaked mustard seeds with 2 green chillies and 2 tbsp water to a smooth paste. Season with a pinch of salt."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Rub cod slices with 0.5 tsp turmeric and 0.5 tsp salt. Set aside 5 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat oil in a wide pan over medium heat. Fry the cod lightly for 2 minutes each side. Remove and set aside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "In the same pan, add nigella seeds and remaining whole green chillies. Fry 30 seconds."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix mustard paste with remaining turmeric and 200ml water. Pour into the pan. Stir and bring to a simmer."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Return the fish to the pan. Spoon sauce over it. Cover and cook on low heat for 8 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Serve with steamed rice. The sauce should be thin and pungent."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Mustard paste is extremely bitter",
              "cause": "Black mustard seeds used in too high a ratio or not soaked long enough",
              "fix": "Use more yellow than black seeds. Soak for at least 30 minutes. A spoonful of yoghurt in the paste also softens the bitterness."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Fish falls apart during cooking",
              "cause": "Fish was moved or stirred in the sauce",
              "fix": "Leave the fish undisturbed after placing it in the sauce. Cod is more delicate than hilsa and breaks easily."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ilish is so deeply embedded in Bengali identity that it is the national fish of Bangladesh. Shorshe ilish is made for the Bengali new year, monsoon celebrations, and family gatherings. The Padma River variety of hilsa is considered the best, with a naturally oily flesh that absorbs the mustard sauce. Since ilish is rarely available outside the region, mackerel or salmon are closer substitutes than cod in terms of fat content, though cod is more widely stocked."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}